               <head>Bustān al-ʿārifīn by Abū al-Layth al-Samarqandī</head>
               <msContents>
                  <summary>Copy of the Sufi treatise Bustān al-ʿārifīn by the
                     10th-century Ḥanafī scholar Abū al-Layth al-Samarqandī, on spiritual and moral
                     conduct. Incomplete at the beginning and the end.</summary>
                  <msItem xml:id="UOL_MS_277-item1">
                     <author key="person_51676273">
                        <persName xml:lang="ar-Latn-x-lc">Abū al-Layth Naṣr ibn Muḥammad
                           al-Samarqandī</persName>
                        <persName xml:lang="ar">ابو الليث نصر بن محمد السمرقندي</persName>
                     </author>
                     <title xml:lang="ar-Latn-x-lc" key="work_1630">Bustān al-ʿārifīn</title>
                     <title xml:lang="ar" key="work_1630">بستان العارفين</title>
                     <incipit xml:lang="ar">الحمد لله رب العالمين و العاقبة للمتقين… قال الشيخ
                        الامام الفقيه ابوالليث نصر بن محمد بن ابراهيم السمرقندي</incipit>
                     <explicit xml:lang="ar">أنه قال من عطس ثلاث عطسات متواليات استقر الايمان في
                        قلبه</explicit>
                     <colophon>Undated and unsigned. The colophon closes with the Persian verse
                           <quote xml:lang="fa">تمت تمام شد / کار من نظام شد / هندو مسلمان
                           شد</quote>.</colophon>
                     <note>
                        <p>Acephalous: the text begins in the middle of the table of contents
                           (sections 24–118, ff. 1r–3r) and breaks off abruptly at the start of
                           chapter 100 (<title xml:lang="ar-Latn-x-lc">Tasmīt al-ʿāṭis</title>). The
                           title is given as <title xml:lang="ar-Latn-x-lc">Kitāb al-Bustān</title>
                           in the preface (f. 5r). The colophon survives on the final leaf, which is
                           pasted to the rear board. Folio references count from the first surviving
                           leaf.</p>
                     </note>
                     <textLang mainLang="ar">Arabic</textLang>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
